INSERT INTO comments ("id", "image_id", "commenter_id", "raw_comment", "comment", "date", "edited", "made_during_challenge") VALUES
(173311, 9803, 3294, '<td valign="top">Let''s count how many times people say this would have been great for the Motion challenge... hehe  <br/> <br/>The b/w works perfectly here.  Would have liked better lighting, but I love the messiness of this.  (8)</td>', 'Let''s count how many times people say this would have been great for the Motion challenge... hehe   The b/w works perfectly here.  Would have liked better lighting, but I love the messiness of this.  (8)', '2002-12-16 11:57:47.000000', NULL, 1),
(173312, 9731, 3294, '<td valign="top">For some reason the photo looks grainy and choppy... resizing issues?  Dunno.</td>', 'For some reason the photo looks grainy and choppy... resizing issues?  Dunno.', '2002-12-16 11:58:50.000000', NULL, 1),
(173315, 9770, 3294, '<td valign="top">Oooo!  Pretty colors! Did you try it with a higher shuter speed?  Might have looked cool with everything frozen maybe?  (7)</td>', 'Oooo!  Pretty colors! Did you try it with a higher shuter speed?  Might have looked cool with everything frozen maybe?  (7)', '2002-12-16 12:03:35.000000', NULL, 1),
(173321, 9622, 4514, '<td valign="top">1)Does the photo meet the challenge?(6)<br/>2)Color:(5)<br/>3)Composition:(5)<br/>4)Focus:(6)<br/>5)Background:(5)<br/>6)Lighting:(4)<br/> <br/>Overall Score:(5.1 Rounded to 5.0)<br/> <br/>Commentary:<br/>I think the Idea here is good.  The real problem in my oppinion is the light.  There is a major glare on the edge of the furn.  With on camera lighting there is little that can be done.  Especially if you have a point and shoot Cam.  The best thing I can say is diffuse this flash with something but if you do that with a point and shoot then the metering will not be right for the cam to take the picture.  Do not know what to say.  <br/> <br/>John (TurboTech)</td>', '1)Does the photo meet the challenge?(6)2)Color:(5)3)Composition:(5)4)Focus:(6)5)Background:(5)6)Lighting:(4) Overall Score:(5.1 Rounded to 5.0) Commentary:I think the Idea here is good.  The real problem in my oppinion is the light.  There is a major glare on the edge of the furn.  With on camera lighting there is little that can be done.  Especially if you have a point and shoot Cam.  The best thing I can say is diffuse this flash with something but if you do that with a point and shoot then the metering will not be right for the cam to take the picture.  Do not know what to say.   John (TurboTech)', '2002-12-16 12:26:35.000000', NULL, 1),
(173328, 9806, 4514, '<td valign="top">1)Does the photo meet the challenge?(4)<br/>2)Color:(5)<br/>3)Composition:(5)<br/>4)Focus:(4)<br/>5)Background:(4)<br/>6)Lighting:(5)<br/> <br/>Overall Score:(4.5 rounded to 5)<br/> <br/>Commentary:<br/>This is a great shot in the making.  I think the buildings in the background take a way from it.  Personally I would have framed it with the subjects a little higher.  I realize you were trying to establish a mood with the background but, but I would not worry so much about what is going on behind as what is going on in front.  That look on the childs face is Candid and that is what is important.  This is a good shot to send to Grandma.  <br/> <br/>John (TuboTech)</td>', '1)Does the photo meet the challenge?(4)2)Color:(5)3)Composition:(5)4)Focus:(4)5)Background:(4)6)Lighting:(5) Overall Score:(4.5 rounded to 5) Commentary:This is a great shot in the making.  I think the buildings in the background take a way from it.  Personally I would have framed it with the subjects a little higher.  I realize you were trying to establish a mood with the background but, but I would not worry so much about what is going on behind as what is going on in front.  That look on the childs face is Candid and that is what is important.  This is a good shot to send to Grandma.   John (TuboTech)', '2002-12-16 12:42:48.000000', NULL, 1),
(173332, 9796, 4514, '<td valign="top">1)Does the photo meet the challenge?(6)<br/>2)Color:(4)<br/>3)Composition:(4)<br/>4)Focus:(3)<br/>5)Background:(4)<br/>6)Lighting:(5)<br/> <br/>Overall Score:(4.3 rounded to 4)<br/> <br/>Commentary:<br/>This was a good try.  The cuffs a tad out of focus, but this is a Macro shot of some sorts so you do not have much room to play with.  My question is, did you want to blur the picture so you could not read the badge?  I can understand that.<br/>Besides that the picture is slightly grainy.  <br/> <br/>John (TurboTech)</td>', '1)Does the photo meet the challenge?(6)2)Color:(4)3)Composition:(4)4)Focus:(3)5)Background:(4)6)Lighting:(5) Overall Score:(4.3 rounded to 4) Commentary:This was a good try.  The cuffs a tad out of focus, but this is a Macro shot of some sorts so you do not have much room to play with.  My question is, did you want to blur the picture so you could not read the badge?  I can understand that.Besides that the picture is slightly grainy.   John (TurboTech)', '2002-12-16 12:53:10.000000', NULL, 1),
