(226403, 9612, 1005, '<td valign="top">Rod, I gave this shot a 9.  I was both impressed by the photo and work behind it, very valuable.  I hope you do find a cure and get a huge medal for it!  (Would this put you in the running for a Nobel?)  I like the transparency in front, places the chemical compounds on the microscope.  Very creative and ties the two together nicely.  The syringe in front might be a little "over the top", but does add a good opposing color releif, so it does have it''s benefits.  <br/>Sorry I didn''t comment this during the challenge week.  I try to comment from the bottom up (this is a learning site, right?), so it''s often a Martha Stewart "good thing" to not get a comment from me!</td>', 'Rod, I gave this shot a 9.  I was both impressed by the photo and work behind it, very valuable.  I hope you do find a cure and get a huge medal for it!  (Would this put you in the running for a Nobel?)  I like the transparency in front, places the chemical compounds on the microscope.  Very creative and ties the two together nicely.  The syringe in front might be a little "over the top", but does add a good opposing color releif, so it does have it''s benefits.  Sorry I didn''t comment this during the challenge week.  I try to comment from the bottom up (this is a learning site, right?), so it''s often a Martha Stewart "good thing" to not get a comment from me!', '2003-03-01 15:23:16.000000', NULL, 0),
